S600 iterated-log scale-law atlas

ABSTRACTION
  If a proof has savings eps_j over scale levels, then residual
  survival is product_j(1-eps_j) <= exp(-sum_j eps_j).
  log/loglog/logloglog are bookkeeping for how many independent
  scale currencies survive after one, two, or three compressions.

TEMPLATES
  scale_harmonic             prod_{j<=J}(1-a/j) <= J^{-a+o(1)}                              ordinary dyadic scale dividend
  compressed_harmonic        prod_{j<=J}(1-a/(j log j)) <= (log J)^{-a+o(1)}                one compressed scale ladder; loglog when J is log N
  meta_compressed_harmonic   prod_{j<=J}(1-a/(j log j loglog j)) <= (loglog J)^{-a+o(1)}    two compressed ladders; logloglog when J is log N
  Tao_shape_unit             log k / (k^2 (loglog k)^2)                                     second-moment overlap dividend spread over compressed scales
  third_log_tax              Tao_shape / logloglog k                                        one extra unresolved meta-scale tax
  third_log_dividend         Tao_shape * logloglog k                                        possible if meta-scale blocks are independently profitable

