OWN INEQUALITY TEMPLATES
1. Meta-scale dividend template:
   If a second-moment proof has one profitable block in each
   logloglog k independent meta-scale class, try surplus
   >= c log k logloglog k / (k^2 (loglog k)^2).
2. Rank-tax template:
   If r unresolved orthogonal scale channels must all be paid, replace
   loglog k by loglog k + r logloglog k in the denominator.
3. Residual-core product template:
   If a sieve-covered residual exports alpha/(j log j) frontier mass
   on compressed scale j, its unresolved mass falls like (log J)^(-alpha).
4. Helly-scale template:
   If every live automaton state of size M has a witness among the first
   H(M) determinant rows, then global CRT search can be replaced by
   a sum over H(M); loglog factors come from harmonic H(M), not from time.

ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE
  Vertices considered: integers, primes, denominator scales, prime blocks,
  proof obligations, determinant rows, residual packets, and entropy channels.
  Chosen vertices: scale currencies.  This preserves where logarithmic
  losses are paid and destroys the original object labels.
